# The widening `(x):type` names a type the way an annotation does, and the
# check that refuses `x:banana` walked parameters only, so it never read one.
# `kanso check` answered ok and left the three engines to speak for
# themselves: the native backend and the page refused the whole program with
# `unknown type`, in a message about a backend, and the interpreter said at
# run time that the value was not a banana — which is true of nothing, since
# no banana exists to compare it against.
fn widen v
  (v):banana

fn also v
  (v):mango

pub play = print "{widen 1} {also 2}"
